@page "/components/kanban"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.Kanban

<DocsHeader Title="Kanban board" Eyebrow="Boards">
    <Lead>Columns of cards that move by dragging, by touch and with the keyboard.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<DocExample Type="typeof(TaskBoard)">
    <p>
        <code>StilKanban</code> shows <code>Items</code> in <code>Columns</code> by the <code>Column</code> selector, in the
        order of <code>Items</code>. Drag a card to another place or column; the line shows where it lands, and Escape
        cancels. With the keyboard, Tab or the arrow keys move between cards, Space picks one up, the arrow keys move it
        and Space drops it (Escape puts it back), and each step is announced to screen readers.
    </p>
    <p>
        The board does not change your data: <code>OnCardMove</code> gets a <code>StilKanbanMove</code> with the item, the
        columns, its place, and the cards before and after it. <code>ApplyTo</code> applies it to a list in board order.
        A column's <code>Limit</code> marks it when it holds more cards (a WIP limit), and the button by its title collapses
        it (<code>CollapsedColumns</code> sets which start collapsed). <code>CardTemplate</code> sets the content of a card;
        without it, <code>Title</code> is shown. Needs an interactive render mode; set
        <code>--stil-kanban-column-width</code> (18rem) and <code>--stil-kanban-height</code> to size it.
    </p>
</DocExample>

